# Volt Browser Rules & Constraints

Always adhere to these guidelines during development:

## 1. Electron Security Hardening
- `contextIsolation: true` is mandatory in the main window.
- `nodeIntegration: false` in the renderer.
- `sandbox: true` enabled.
- Sanitize and validate all IPC channel inputs and schemas.

## 2. Front-End Architecture
- Use React 19, TypeScript, Vite, and Vanilla CSS.
- Strictly avoid `any` types. Ensure full type safety.
- Apply macOS/glassmorphism aesthetics. Use CSS variables for colors.
- Use `width: 0px; height: 0px;` and `visibility: hidden;` for background webviews to prevent CPU drain while maintaining websocket sessions.

## 3. WebView Preload Script Constraints
- Preload attribute on `<webview>` must be provided in the initial React render.
- Preload path must be resolved asynchronously on startup by the main process and copied to the real filesystem (`app.getPath('userData')`) in production due to ASAR loading restrictions.

## 4. Git & Workflow
- Use conventional commits: `feat(...)`, `fix(...)`, `chore(...)`.
- Work on feature branches (`feature/<name>`). Never commit directly to `main`.
- Always verify build succeeds before pushing: `npm run build`.

## 5. Build Lock Prevention
- Ensure all instances of `Volt Browser` and `electron` are stopped before executing `npm run dist` using `scripts/check-release-locks.mjs`.
